    <p>
      <b>Description</b>
    </p>
    <p>Combines input port 1 (real part) and input port 2 (imaginary part) into one complex output signal.</p>
    <p>Complexity is a per-port attribute orthogonal to the numeric type: the complex signal flows through the complex-aware math blocks (gain, sum, mult, divide, negate, conjugate) and the routing blocks, and back to real signals through <code>complexToRealImag</code>, <code>complexToMagnitudeAngle</code> or <code>abs</code> (magnitude).</p>
    <p>This page describes the native runtime behavior observed in the module C++ sources. Declared phases indicate when the simulation engine calls the block.</p>
    <p>Code generation: supported for C and Rust.</p>
